course: dictionary
lesson: 2894
title: Doubly: twice over
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Doubly means twice, or in two ways. When you meet «doubly sure», the clue is that the person checked twice, so it means very sure. Look at the words around the word to find out how it is being used.
explain: In maths, doubly means times two. Doubling 5 gives 10. The same idea of twice as much is used in everyday words: «doubly important» means even more important, and «make doubly sure» means check it again to be certain.
explain: «Uzbekistan is one of only two doubly landlocked countries.» Landlocked means having no sea coast. The clues are «all its neighbours have no sea coast either» and «it must cross two countries to reach an ocean». So doubly landlocked means cut off from the sea in two ways.
fact: Doubly means twice as much, or in two ways.
fact: «Doubly sure» means very sure, because you have checked twice.
fact: In maths, doubly means times two: 5 doubled is 10.
fact: Doubly can also mean even more or especially, as in «doubly important».
fact: «Doubly landlocked» means having no sea coast, and all your neighbours having none either.
exercise: «Uzbekistan is one of only two doubly landlocked countries.» What does doubly mean here? | Boats sail there twice a year | Full of water | *Cut off from the sea in two ways | Very close to the sea
exercise: «She made doubly sure the door was locked.» What does doubly sure mean? | Sure only on Sundays | *Very sure, after checking twice | Sure of nothing | Not sure at all
exercise: In maths, doubly means times two. What is 5 doubled? | 7 | 25 | 2.5 | *10
test: «King Louie is doubly made up» in The Jungle Book. What does doubly suggest? | Made up, but only a little | Written in a book | *Unreal in two ways, since apes cannot talk like us and orangutans do not live in India | Real, and very well known
test: Which phrase means even more important? | *Doubly important | Not important | Important once | Less important
exam: «Kazakhstan is the largest landlocked country in the world, and Uzbekistan is one of only two doubly landlocked countries.» Why must Uzbekistan cross two countries to reach an ocean? | *All its neighbours have no sea coast either, so it must cross two countries | It is an island, so it has boats | Its neighbours have a sea coast, so it can reach the sea easily | It lives on the ocean
